page("carbon-steel-care-in-texas-humidity","Carbon Steel Grill Care in Texas Humidity","Keeping a carbon steel folding grill rust-free in Gulf Coast humidity and summer storms: seasoning, oiling and storage.","balm",f"""
<p>Southeast Texas humidity will find bare carbon steel. Slot Grill's FAQ says light surface rust is purely cosmetic: clean it off and re-season. Better to prevent it.</p>
<h2>After every cook</h2>{ol(["Scrape the grates warm.","Let it cool, empty the ash.","Wipe cooking surfaces with a thin coat of oil or <a href='"+BALM+"'>Slot Grill Seasoning Balm</a>.","Store dry, indoors if you can."])}
<h2>Seasoning</h2><p>Season the cooking surfaces with very thin coats of oil or balm, heated to cure; Slot Grill's balm page says 400°F for 1 hour, repeated as needed. Slot Grill's FAQ says the makers like high-temperature BBQ paint on the body, and the balm page calls balm a food-safe alternative for the body. Never paint grates or griddles.</p>
<h2>Fixing rust</h2><p>Scrub with steel wool to dark steel, wipe, oil thinly, heat to cure.</p>
""","gear",[])

page("made-in-buna-texas","Made in Buna, Texas","Where the Slot Grill is made: by Keith in Buna, in Southeast Texas, from thick carbon steel.","c13",f"""
<p>Buna is a small town in Jasper County, in the Piney Woods of Southeast Texas. It's where Keith makes the Slot Grill.</p>
<p>According to Slot Grill's <a href="{MADE}">Made in USA page</a>, Slot Grills are made by Keith in Buna, Texas, and during times of very high demand, U.S.-based business partners help with manufacturing, so every Slot Grill is made in the USA. Slot Grill's About page says development and production began in 2024, and the design has been refined through real-world use since.</p>
<h2>What it's made of</h2><p>Thick carbon steel: 10-gauge on the Full Size, 12-gauge on the Compact. Tab-and-slot assembly by hand, no tools, no hinges. There's no stainless model.</p>
<h2>Where to buy</h2><p>Slot Grill sells direct at <a href="{HOME}">SlotGrill.com</a>, the @SlotGrill TikTok Shop and @SlotGrill on the Shop app, and says it has no authorized third-party resellers.</p>
""","gear",[])

page("hauling-a-folding-grill-in-a-truck-or-utv","Hauling a Folding Grill in a Truck, UTV or Boat","How to carry a flat-pack charcoal grill in a pickup, side-by-side or boat, and why you never cook on the vehicle.","full01",f"""
<p>A flat pack rides anywhere: behind a truck seat, in a UTV box, under a boat seat. Slot Grill's FAQ confirms both work in a UTV bed or cargo box and aboard a boat as cargo.</p>
<h2>Carrying</h2>{ul(["Cold and empty only. Never pack a warm grill or ash.","Bag it to keep soot off seats and gear.","Strap it flat so it doesn't slide."])}
<h2>Cooking</h2>{ul(["Set up on the ground, clear of the vehicle, dry grass and anything that can burn.","Never on a truck bed, tailgate, UTV bed or boat deck.","Keep fuel cans far from the fire."])}
""","gear",[])
